IO-03: give negative and NaN rainfall records no rain

A rain time series or a user-prepared rain file accepted any value as a
rainfall record, so a negative missing-data flag such as -1 became negative
rainfall and a "nan" made every result undefined. convertRainfall() now
returns no rain for a negative or NaN record, so getNextRainfall() skips it
like an explicit zero and a cumulative gage keeps its last valid reading.
readStdLine() counts such a value in a user-prepared file as a missing
period (shown in the Rainfall File Summary) instead of saving it.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-03_swmm530.patch

